[{"location":"Constants.html#LensFactory.Constants","page":"Constants","title":"LensFactory.Constants","text":"Constants\n\nTesting :-)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"module"},{"location":"Constants.html#Natural-constants","page":"Constants","title":"Natural constants","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Constants.html","page":"Constants","title":"Constants","text":"CONST_C = 299792458.0                        # meters/s\nCONST_G = 6.6743E-11                         # m^3 kg/s^2","category":"page"},{"location":"Constants.html#Solar-constants","page":"Constants","title":"Solar constants","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Constants.html","page":"Constants","title":"Constants","text":"MASS_SUN = 1.98855E+30                       # kg\nRADIUS_SUN = 696340E+03                      # meters\nLUMINOSITY_SUN = 3.828E26                    # Watts = Joule/s","category":"page"},{"location":"Constants.html#Distance-units","page":"Constants","title":"Distance units","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Constants.html","page":"Constants","title":"Constants","text":"DIST_PC = 3.0856775714409184E+16             # meters\nDIST_KPC = 3.0856775714409184E+19            # meters\nDIST_MPC = 3.0856775714409184E+22            # meters\nDIST_GPC = 3.0856775714409184E+25            # meters","category":"page"},{"location":"Constants.html#Angular-units","page":"Constants","title":"Angular units","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Constants.html","page":"Constants","title":"Constants","text":"ANGLE_MICROARCSEC= 4.848136811095361E-12     # radians\nANGLE_MILLIARCSEC= 4.84813681109536E-09      # radians\nANGLE_ARCSEC = 4.84813681109536E-06          # radians\nANGLE_ARCMIN = 0.0002908882086657216         # radians\nANGLE_DEGREE = 0.017453292519943295          # radians","category":"page"},{"location":"Constants.html#Temporal-units","page":"Constants","title":"Temporal units","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Constants.html","page":"Constants","title":"Constants","text":"YEAR2SECOND = 31557600.0                     # Seconds in a year\nYEAR2HOUR = 8766.0                           # Hours in a year\nYEAR2DAY = 365.25                            # Days in a year\nDAY2HOUR = 24.0                              # Hours in a day\nDAY2SECOND = 86400.0                         # Seconds in a day","category":"page"},{"location":"Cosmology.html#LensFactory.Cosmology","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology","text":"Cosmology\n\nTesting :-)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"module"},{"location":"Cosmology.html#Methods","page":"Cosmology","title":"Methods","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"Cosmology.html#LensFactory.Cosmology.init_cosmology","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.init_cosmology","text":"init_cosmology\n\nAn Abstract type to initialize cosmology.\n\nArguments\n\nH0::Union{Int64, Float64} = 70.0: Hubble constant, in km/s/Mpc\nw::Union{Int64, Float64} = -1.0: Dark energy EOS parameter\nΩ_m0::Union{Int64, Float64} = 0.3: Present matter density parameter\nΩ_r0::Union{Int64, Float64} = 0.0: Present radiation density parameter\nΩ_w0::Union{Int64, Float64} = 0.7: Present dark energy density parameter\n\nReturns\n\ncosmology::AbstractCosmology: Cosmology instance defined by the input parameters\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"type"},{"location":"Cosmology.html#LensFactory.Cosmology.scale_factor","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.scale_factor","text":"scale_factor(z)\n\nCalculates the scale factor at a given redshift.\n\nFormula: a = 1  (1+z)\n\nArguments\n\nz::Union{Int64, Float64}: Redshift\n\nReturns\n\nUnion{Int64, Float64}: Scale factor\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology.html#LensFactory.Cosmology.hubble_time","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.hubble_time","text":"hubble_time(H0)\n\nCalculates age of the Universe.\n\nFormula: t_H = 1  rm H_0\n\nArguments\n\nH0::Union{Int64, Float64}: Hubble constant, in km/s/Mpc\n\nReturns\n\nUnion{Int64, Float64}: Age of the Universe, in Gyr\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology.html#LensFactory.Cosmology.hubble_parameter","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.hubble_parameter","text":"hubble_parameter(cosmology, z)\n\nCalculates Hubble parameter at redshift z.\n\nFormula: \n\nArguments\n\ncosmology::AbstractCosmology: Cosmology instance\nz::Union{Int64, Float64}: Input redshift\n\nReturns\n\nUnion{Int64, Float64}: Hubble parameter at redshift z, in km/s/Mpc\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology.html#LensFactory.Cosmology.hubble_distance","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.hubble_distance","text":"hubble_distance(H0)\n\nCalculates radius of the observable Universe.\n\nFormula: R_H = crm H_0\n\nArguments\n\nH0::Union{Int64, Float64}: Hubble constant, in km/s/Mpc\n\nReturns\n\nUnion{Int64, Float64}: Radius of the observable Universe, in meters \n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology.html#LensFactory.Cosmology.distance_modulus","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.distance_modulus","text":"distance_modulus(cosmology, z)\n\nCalculates the distance modulus to a given redshift z.\n\nFormula: \\mu = 5 \\log(d) - 5\n\nArguments\n\ncosmology::AbstractCosmology: Cosmology instance\nz::Union{Int64, Float64}: Input redshift\n\nReturns\n\nUnion{Int64, Float64}: Distance modulus to a redshift z\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology.html#LensFactory.Cosmology.rho_cz","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.rho_cz","text":"rho_cz(cosmology, z)\n\nCalculates the critical density of the Universe at redshift z.\n\nFormula: rho_c(z) = frac3 H^2(z)8 pi rm G `\n\nArguments\n\ncosmology::AbstractCosmology: Cosmology instance\nz::Union{Int64, Float64}: Input redshift\n\nReturns\n\nUnion{Int64, Float64}: Critical density at redshift z\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology.html#LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_mz","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_mz","text":"Omega_mz(cosmology, z)\n\nCalculates the matter density parameter at redshift z.\n\nFormula: Ω_mz = Ω_m0 * (1+z)^3 * (H0/H(z))^2\n\nArguments\n\ncosmology::AbstractCosmology: Cosmology instance\nz::Union{Int64, Float64}: Input redshift\n\nReturns\n\nUnion{Int64, Float64}: Matter density parameter at redshift z\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology.html#LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_rz","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_rz","text":"Omega_rz(cosmology, z)\n\nCalculates the radiation density parameter at redshift z.\n\nFormula: Ω_rz = Ω_r0 * (1+z)^4 * (H0/H(z))^2\n\nArguments\n\ncosmology::AbstractCosmology: Cosmology instance\nz::Union{Int64, Float64}: Input redshift\n\nReturns\n\nUnion{Int64, Float64}: Radiation density parameter at redshift z\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology.html#LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_wz","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_wz","text":"Omega_wz(cosmology, z)\n\nCalculates the dark energy density parameter at redshift z.\n\nFormula: Ω_wz = Ω_w0 * (1+z)^(3*(1+w)) * (H0/H(z))^2\n\nArguments\n\ncosmology::AbstractCosmology: Cosmology instance\nz::Union{Int64, Float64}: Input redshift\n\nReturns\n\nUnion{Int64, Float64}: Dark energy density parameter at redshift z\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology.html#LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_kz","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.Omega_kz","text":"Omega_kz(cosmology, z)\n\nCalculates the curvature density parameter at redshift z.\n\nFormula: Ω_kz = Ω_k0 * (1+z)^2 * (H0/H(z))^2\n\nArguments\n\ncosmology::AbstractCosmology: Cosmology instance\nz::Union{Int64, Float64}: Input redshift\n\nReturns\n\nUnion{Int64, Float64}: Curvature density parameter at redshift z\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology.html#LensFactory.Cosmology.lookback_time","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.lookback_time","text":"lookback_time(cosmology, z)\n\nCalculates lookbak time for a given redshift z\n\nFormula: $ tL(z) = \\int0^z \\frac{1}{(1+z')H(z')} dz' $\n\nArguments\n\ncosmology::AbstractCosmology: Cosmology instance\nz::Union{Int64, Float64}: Input redshift\n\nReturns\n\nUnion{Int64, Float64}: Lookback time for a source at redshift z\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"Cosmology.html#LensFactory.Cosmology.comoving_volume_element","page":"Cosmology","title":"LensFactory.Cosmology.comoving_volume_element","text":"comovingvolumeelement(cosmology, z)\n\nCalculates the comving volume element at redshift z, in Gpc^3.\n\nFormula: $ dV = dH \\frac{D_M^2}{E(z)} $\n\nArguments\n\ncosmology::AbstractCosmology: Cosmology instance\nz::Union{Int64, Float64}: Input redshift\n\nReturns\n\nUnion{Int64, Float64}: Comoving volume element at redshift z, in Gpc^3\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"function"},{"location":"index.html#LensFactory.jl","page":"Home","title":"LensFactory.jl","text":"","category":"section"},{"location":"index.html","page":"Home","title":"Home","text":"Documentation for LensFactory.jl","category":"page"},{"location":"index.html#LensFactory","page":"Home","title":"LensFactory","text":"LensFactory\n\nTesting :-)\n\n\n\n\n\n","category":"module"}]
